source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-23
observed: Every `|` inside `[...]` stays with the link; the row is two cells. Jira reads the third part as the link title and resolves nothing for the target it is left with.
-- input.jira --
||h1||h2||
|[a|b|c]|d|
-- rendered.html --
<div class='table-wrap'>
<table class='confluenceTable'><tbody>
<tr>
<th class='confluenceTh'>h1</th>
<th class='confluenceTh'>h2</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'><span class="error">&#91;a|b|c&#93;</span></td>
<td class='confluenceTd'>d</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
</div>
-- want.md --
:::table
||h1||h2||
|[a|b|c]|d|
:::
-- warnings.json --
[]
